@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        var returnUrl = Navigation.ToBaseRelativePath(Navigation.Uri);
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(returnUrl) || returnUrl == "/")
            returnUrl = "/";

        Navigation.NavigateTo($"/Account/Login?returnUrl={Uri.EscapeDataString(returnUrl)}",
                             forceLoad: true);
    }
}


<!--
Why forceLoad Is Critical for Login
Let's trace a login flow WITHOUT forceLoad:

1. User is on /Login page
2. User enters username + password, clicks "Log in"
3. Blazor sends the form data over SignalR to server
4. Server validates credentials: "Correct. Here's an authentication cookie."
5. Server sends the cookie back in the SignalR response
6. Browser receives the cookie and stores it
7. Blazor code: Navigation.NavigateTo("/"); // Default navigation
8. Blazor updates the virtual DOM to show the home page
9. BUT: The SignalR circuit was created BEFORE the cookie existed
10. The circuit's authentication state still says: "Anonymous user"
11. Home page renders as if user is NOT logged in
12. User: "I just logged in! Why can't I see anything?!"

Now WITH forceLoad:

1. User logs in (same steps 1-6)
2. Server sends cookie
3. Blazor code: Navigation.NavigateTo("/", forceLoad: true);
4. Browser does a REAL HTTP GET request to /
5. Server receives request WITH the new cookie
6. Server: "I see the authentication cookie. User is John. Show home page."
7. Server sends full HTML
8. SignalR circuit is created fresh with the cookie already present
9. Authentication state: "John Doe, authenticated"
10. Home page renders correctly
11. User: "I'm logged in. Everything works."
-->